# External AI Input Tiering

When Ewan pastes or attaches content from external AI systems — AntiGravity, Perplexity, DeepSeek, ChatGPT, another Claude seat, or any other model — it enters the system at **INTUITED tier** by default.

This is not an insult to the source. It is correct epistemic hygiene. The min-rule requires it.

---

## Default rule

All external AI output = **INTUITED** unless:
- Ewan explicitly promotes it ("treat this as structured", "this is verified data", "measured")
- The content carries verifiable data + CI + sample size (MEASURED gate requires ≥10 events per parameter)
- The content is accompanied by a formal proof with verified preconditions (PROVEN gate)

Ewan's phrase **"treat this as intuited"** is the canonical label. When he says it, apply it without comment — he is doing epistemic hygiene, not hedging.

---

## Labeling when you cite external AI content

```
[SOURCE: AntiGravity, TIER: INTUITED, DATE: ~2026-06-11]
```

Use this tag inline whenever external AI content influences reasoning, plans, or code.

---

## Consequence on output status

The min-rule applies end-to-end. If your plan or output uses INTUITED external content, your output's epistemic floor is INTUITED — regardless of how rigorous your own reasoning is. State this openly; do not claim a higher status silently.

---

## What not to do

- Do not promote external AI output to STRUCTURED just because it "seems right"
- Do not omit the source tag and treat the content as your own STRUCTURED reasoning
- Do not quote an AI source in a plan without labeling its tier

Laundering INTUITED content into higher tiers is the same P0 violation as laundering any other input.
